WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.205
One more project that I would like to

00:00:01.205 --> 00:00:03.455
leave you with... that is what I am

00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:05.825
planning to do next. And I haven't yet

00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:08.075
talked about this. This is the first time that

00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:11.375
I am saying anything at all about it.

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:16.055
What I am planning to do is to create

00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:18.905
a calendar. There are a lot of those.

00:00:18.905 --> 00:00:22.774
The Gregorian calendar for example. And the

00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:27.425
calendars that we have are very regular.

00:00:27.425 --> 00:00:30.395
They are more regular than the spin of

00:00:30.395 --> 00:00:31.715
the planet. They're certainly more

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:34.835
regular than life on Earth. And so that

00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:37.355
got me thinking about whether you could

00:00:37.355 --> 00:00:39.515
have a different kind of a calendar.

00:00:39.515 --> 00:00:43.505
A calendar that would in fact be true to

00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:46.265
life in terms of the fact that it would

00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:48.544
keep time according to how life was

00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:50.735
lived on this planet. Well those

00:00:50.735 --> 00:00:52.445
calendars are actually all around us.

00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:55.055
They're called trees. And trees will grow

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.215
a ring every year. And the girth of that

00:00:57.215 --> 00:00:59.824
ring is determined by climate, by

00:00:59.824 --> 00:01:02.615
rainfall, weather patterns, and so forth.

00:01:02.615 --> 00:01:04.795
But we don't tend to see them in that

00:01:04.795 --> 00:01:07.235
way unless we saw them down.

00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:10.535
And to me it seems that you could in fact

00:01:10.595 --> 00:01:16.215
make a tree operate as a calendar by taking that tree--

00:01:16.215 --> 00:01:18.775
and I am proposing a bristlecone pine,

00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:21.635
a tree with a 5,000 year lifespan--

00:01:21.635 --> 00:01:24.595
and putting milestones around it.

00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:27.435
Well, not exactly milestones, but

00:01:27.535 --> 00:01:30.775
"century stones." Or stones with a 500 year period

00:01:30.784 --> 00:01:33.335
between stones, set at regular intervals

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:36.125
according to... if the calendar, if the

00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:37.775
tree were to grow at the rate that it

00:01:37.775 --> 00:01:40.635
is right now where would it be in 500 years?

00:01:40.755 --> 00:01:43.415
At that point it will grow large enough

00:01:43.415 --> 00:01:45.935
that because of its strength it will

00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:47.824
turn over that stone. And a thousand

00:01:47.824 --> 00:01:50.884
years... and so forth up to 5,000. But

00:01:50.884 --> 00:01:53.945
of course it will fall out of sync.

00:01:53.945 --> 00:01:57.545
It won't won't work out that that 500 years

00:01:57.545 --> 00:01:59.345
will be the same 500 years as you have

00:01:59.345 --> 00:02:03.454
marked on your Gregorian calendar. And

00:02:03.454 --> 00:02:04.835
to me that is where it really

00:02:04.835 --> 00:02:07.055
gets interesting. Because I don't know which

00:02:07.055 --> 00:02:08.795
calendar in that case

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.195
we would say was right. I don't know

00:02:11.195 --> 00:02:15.305
how we would account for time if we

00:02:15.305 --> 00:02:17.374
had these two different kinds of calendars

00:02:17.374 --> 00:02:20.225
that were simultaneously keeping time.

00:02:20.225 --> 00:02:22.085
One of which was celestial; one of which

00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:24.484
was abstract. And the other of which was

00:02:24.484 --> 00:02:27.214
manifestly terrestrial and

00:02:27.215 --> 00:02:30.605
was really about the world as we exist in it.

00:02:30.755 --> 00:02:32.695
The world in which we are living in now.

00:02:32.695 --> 00:02:37.055
So where to get a bristlecone pine?

00:02:37.055 --> 00:02:41.464
Well it just so happens that I know some

00:02:41.464 --> 00:02:43.654
people who have more than one of them.

00:02:43.654 --> 00:02:46.805
The Long Now Foundation happens to

00:02:46.805 --> 00:02:51.035
have this space... more than a space, it's

00:02:51.035 --> 00:02:53.825
800 odd acres in Eastern Nevada:

00:02:53.825 --> 00:02:56.675
Mount Washington. They bought it back in

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:59.165
the 01990s. And it just so happens to have

00:02:59.165 --> 00:03:01.795
the world's largest bristlecone pine

00:03:01.815 --> 00:03:05.015
forest in private hands.

00:03:05.335 --> 00:03:08.455
This is the ideal space and I've already started

00:03:08.455 --> 00:03:10.475
talking with The Long Now Foundation

00:03:10.475 --> 00:03:12.775
about how we might implement this. To put

00:03:12.785 --> 00:03:15.755
the calendar there that would be

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.154
able for the next five thousand years

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.000
to keep time on our planet.

